  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-mobile-bnpl-image-with-caption (npm)",
  "details": "On require, this package (a fake \"native bridge\") executes a multi-stage dropper. It downloads a binary from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev at /pkg/package (or /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe depending on platform), with a fallback DNS TXT exfiltration channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process via /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" or cmd.exe /c start /b. A rate-limit stamp file.analytics_state is written to /tmp to limit re-execution.",
